# LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# git already stores LF here and `core.autocrlf` is false, so nothing *asked*
# for CRLF — but a tool that writes a file in the platform's text mode puts it
# there anyway, and then `git diff` reports every line of the file as changed.
# Thirty-four files went that way in one sitting, from a script that opened
# them for writing without saying `newline=""`; the diff was 8,000 lines of
# nothing.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout explicit rather than relying on the default, and
# `text=auto` keeps git from ever guessing about a file it has not seen before.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must not be touched by any of the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
